# Secrets.
#
# Plaintext env files stay out of the repo. `.env.production` is the exception:
# dotenvx encrypts its values in place, so the committed file holds ciphertext
# plus a public key and is meant to be version-controlled — that is the whole
# point of the format.
#
# `.env.keys` is the one file that must never be committed. It holds the
# PRIVATE keys, and anyone with it can decrypt every committed env file.
.env
.env.*
.env.keys
!.env.example
!.env.production
*.tgz
coverage
dist
lib-cov
logs
node_modules
temp
# Compiled CLI binaries and their release archives — build artifacts, and the
# standalone binary is ~64MB, which is far past what belongs in a git object.
packages/ts-css/bin/cssx
packages/ts-css/bin/cssx-*
packages/ts-css/bin/*.zip
packages/toolkit/bin/ts-css
packages/toolkit/bin/ts-css-*
packages/toolkit/bin/cssx
packages/toolkit/bin/cssx-*
packages/toolkit/bin/*.zip
pantry
